WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.040 --> 00:00:03.056
[upbeat techno music plays]

00:00:03.080 --> 00:00:05.700
♪♪

00:00:09.870 --> 00:00:12.156
-[Caine]: Today's adventure
is brought to you

00:00:12.180 --> 00:00:15.076
by the Favorite Character Awards!

00:00:15.100 --> 00:00:20.286
Stay tuned and find out
who will claim the ultimate prize!

00:00:20.310 --> 00:00:23.290
[glitzy orchestral music plays]

00:00:23.320 --> 00:00:25.333
[inaudible chatter]

00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:27.466
-[Zooble]: [BOINK!]

00:00:27.490 --> 00:00:29.296
Can you toss that back up here?

00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:31.376
-[scoffs] Making good use
of your parts gimmick, huh?

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:33.036
-[Zooble]: Oh, shut up.

00:00:33.060 --> 00:00:34.466
-What are you doing up there?

00:00:34.490 --> 00:00:35.996
-[Zooble]: I'm hiding from Caine.

00:00:36.020 --> 00:00:37.996
I think I overheard him
talking to Bubble

00:00:38.020 --> 00:00:40.216
about an in-house adventure,

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:42.786
and I'm not gonna be part of it.

00:00:42.810 --> 00:00:46.686
-And... you're just gonna
hang out in a flower pot all day?

00:00:46.710 --> 00:00:48.066
Not, like, your room?

00:00:48.090 --> 00:00:50.816
-[Zooble]: Caine's been checking up
on my room lately.

00:00:50.840 --> 00:00:54.096
When I don't answer,
he just starts singing "Daisy Bell"

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:55.676
in front of my door.

00:00:55.700 --> 00:00:57.166
It's creepy.

00:00:57.190 --> 00:00:58.726
-Does he really do that?

00:00:58.750 --> 00:01:00.366
-I dunno.
Let's ask him.

00:01:00.390 --> 00:01:01.746
[hollers]
Hey, Caine!

00:01:01.770 --> 00:01:03.516
-[Zooble]:
You [BOINK!] [BANG!]hole!

00:01:03.540 --> 00:01:04.626
-Yes, Jax?

00:01:04.650 --> 00:01:06.066
-Look, it's Zooble!

00:01:06.090 --> 00:01:08.256
-[Zooble]: [BOINK!] you!
-Ah, there you are!

00:01:08.280 --> 00:01:10.323
Now I don't have to do
the snap-summon thing.

00:01:11.543 --> 00:01:13.816
-[Zooble]: [grunts]
-And I'm glad I found you.

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:16.606
We need even numbers,
'cause today's adventure is a...

00:01:16.630 --> 00:01:18.766
[overlapping voices]
TEAM adventure!

00:01:18.790 --> 00:01:20.906
[normal voice]
Meet you guys up at the stage in, uh --

00:01:20.930 --> 00:01:23.283
let's say 5.7 minutes.

00:01:24.870 --> 00:01:26.160
-[Zooble]: Great.

00:01:27.570 --> 00:01:30.166
You didn't even ask him
about the singing thing.

00:01:30.190 --> 00:01:31.190
-The what?

00:01:32.080 --> 00:01:35.736
-Today's adventure is...
gonna be a bit of a short one,

00:01:35.760 --> 00:01:38.466
due to the Favorite Character Awards.

00:01:38.490 --> 00:01:40.196
But it'll be
a perfect opportunity

00:01:40.220 --> 00:01:43.606
to showcase your guys' strengths
to the press!

00:01:43.630 --> 00:01:46.076
-This is so heavy.
-That's right, Bubble.

00:01:46.100 --> 00:01:49.166
Seeing you all
play batball a few days ago

00:01:49.190 --> 00:01:50.416
really got me thinking.

00:01:50.440 --> 00:01:52.336
We should do
our own sporting event!

00:01:52.360 --> 00:01:54.236
But with cool new sports

00:01:54.260 --> 00:01:56.516
invented by yours truly.
-Help me, Caine.

00:01:56.540 --> 00:02:00.406
-Uh, we could also just play softball
normally this time.

00:02:00.430 --> 00:02:01.946
-Eeegh...

00:02:01.970 --> 00:02:06.366
-In the Caine Leagues,
we have the 400 Meter Vertical Skedaddle,

00:02:06.390 --> 00:02:08.576
Bisection Boogie Eggball,

00:02:08.600 --> 00:02:11.186
Lateral Hijinks,
Orange Sport,

00:02:11.210 --> 00:02:12.996
Ball Run,
Walk Ball,

00:02:13.020 --> 00:02:15.686
Run Walk,
and Ball Ball!

00:02:15.710 --> 00:02:17.576
These sports are surely going to --

00:02:17.600 --> 00:02:18.845
-[Zooble]: Uh, yeah, sorry, no.

00:02:18.870 --> 00:02:21.376
I'm not gonna be on a team with that one.
-[blows kiss]

00:02:21.400 --> 00:02:24.236
-Zooble, why does all you do
is complaining?

00:02:24.260 --> 00:02:25.736
I never know what you want!

00:02:25.760 --> 00:02:28.386
-[Zooble]: We had a whole
suggestion box for that.

00:02:28.410 --> 00:02:30.326
-Yeah, Zooble and I constantly say

00:02:30.350 --> 00:02:33.186
we like more chill
and relaxing adventures.

00:02:33.210 --> 00:02:35.796
-Did you really
not like my softball one?

00:02:35.820 --> 00:02:38.646
-I'm not big into sports.
Sorry.

00:02:38.670 --> 00:02:41.616
-The suggestion box just causes
interpersonal drama.

00:02:41.640 --> 00:02:43.260
And me no likey.
-[Zooble]: Alright.

00:02:43.290 --> 00:02:46.056
You really wanna know what I want?
-Oh, no.

00:02:46.080 --> 00:02:48.640
-[Zooble]:
I want the ability to have ***.

00:02:49.550 --> 00:02:50.846
-No way.

00:02:50.870 --> 00:02:54.316
Are we FINALLY having
this conversation?

00:02:54.340 --> 00:02:55.946
-[stammers]

00:02:55.970 --> 00:02:57.946
[babbling]
[sinister music plays]

00:02:57.970 --> 00:03:02.416
♪♪

00:03:02.440 --> 00:03:03.440
[ding!]

00:03:04.370 --> 00:03:05.906
Oh.
Hi, Zooble!

00:03:05.930 --> 00:03:08.486
-[Zooble]: Do you have any
of that stupid sauce left?

00:03:08.510 --> 00:03:09.996
-What were we talking about?
Oh, yeah!

00:03:10.020 --> 00:03:13.366
How teamwork is essential
to making the dream work!

00:03:13.390 --> 00:03:14.696
-[Zooble]: Tell that to him!

00:03:14.720 --> 00:03:16.926
He's the one that
[BOINKS!] everything all the time.

00:03:16.950 --> 00:03:18.926
-You are in a mood today,
aren't you?

00:03:18.950 --> 00:03:21.506
-Now, now -- you know
what they say about assuming.

00:03:21.530 --> 00:03:22.750
It makes an "ass"

00:03:22.780 --> 00:03:25.570
out of "u" and "ming."

00:03:25.600 --> 00:03:28.100
-[Zooble]: "Ming"?
-Did Caine just say [BOINK]?"

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:33.166
-[Ming]: Hi, I'm Ming,
and I really don't appreciate

00:03:33.190 --> 00:03:36.060
what your assumptions have done
to my reputation.

00:03:37.400 --> 00:03:39.106
-[Zooble]:
You made a whole guy for that?

00:03:39.130 --> 00:03:41.046
-Whatever the case,
it's evident now

00:03:41.070 --> 00:03:43.706
that there's quite a bit
of tension between you all.

00:03:43.730 --> 00:03:47.326
So, maybe what we actually need to do
are trust exercises!

00:03:47.350 --> 00:03:49.526
-[Zooble]:
I am not falling into Jax's arms,

00:03:49.550 --> 00:03:50.946
if that's what you mean.

00:03:50.970 --> 00:03:53.986
-Don't worry -- this will be
a two-way trust exercise,

00:03:54.010 --> 00:03:55.636
where you'll each have
to trust each other

00:03:55.660 --> 00:03:57.566
to not betray the other person.

00:03:57.590 --> 00:03:59.046
[snap!]
[shwing!]

00:03:59.070 --> 00:04:00.206
This is a private room,

00:04:00.230 --> 00:04:03.986
where nobody can see
or hear you once inside.

00:04:04.010 --> 00:04:05.756
And this...
[shwing!]

00:04:05.780 --> 00:04:07.656
...is a loaded gun!
-Oh, boy.

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:10.286
-Character A will take the gun
into the private room

00:04:10.310 --> 00:04:12.666
and empty it out
of all its ammunition,

00:04:12.690 --> 00:04:15.346
then come out
and give it to Character B.

00:04:15.370 --> 00:04:17.310
Character B will then
take the gun

00:04:17.340 --> 00:04:19.196
and shoot themselves
in the head,

00:04:19.220 --> 00:04:22.786
trusting that Character A emptied it
in the private room.

00:04:22.810 --> 00:04:24.696
Character A will also
have to trust

00:04:24.720 --> 00:04:27.556
that Character B won't
turn the gun on them,

00:04:27.580 --> 00:04:30.566
so everyone is incentivized
to follow the rules

00:04:30.590 --> 00:04:32.126
and trust each other!

00:04:32.150 --> 00:04:34.096
-[Zooble]:
Sounds a little convoluted.

00:04:34.120 --> 00:04:35.106
-YOU LOOK CONVOLUTED!!!!

00:04:35.130 --> 00:04:37.086
Anyway, Jax,
why don't you start?

00:04:37.110 --> 00:04:38.386
-[Zooble]: Wh-- Him?!

00:04:38.410 --> 00:04:40.486
-Wait, what am I doing?
I wasn't paying attention.

00:04:40.510 --> 00:04:42.630
[rewound audio warbling]

00:04:46.030 --> 00:04:47.500
[clicks tongue]
Oh.

00:04:49.450 --> 00:04:50.460
-[yelps]

00:04:51.980 --> 00:04:53.966
-Or, yeah, we could
all just shoot each other.

00:04:53.990 --> 00:04:56.566
Here, have guns.
I don't care anymore.

00:04:56.590 --> 00:04:57.926
-Hooway!

00:04:57.950 --> 00:04:59.226
-[Zooble]: Wait, that's just it?

00:04:59.250 --> 00:05:00.936
"Here's guns, and have fun"?

00:05:00.960 --> 00:05:02.086
-I didn't say "have fun."

00:05:02.110 --> 00:05:04.286
-[Zooble]:
It's just a little aimless.

00:05:04.310 --> 00:05:05.856
-Use the sights.
-[Zooble]: Caine!

00:05:05.880 --> 00:05:07.416
-[growls]
FINE!

00:05:07.440 --> 00:05:08.796
We're bringing teams back.

00:05:08.820 --> 00:05:10.156
Pair up in teams of two.

00:05:10.180 --> 00:05:11.446
You all get three lives.

00:05:11.470 --> 00:05:13.276
Last team surviving
is the winner.

00:05:13.300 --> 00:05:14.456
Happy?

00:05:14.480 --> 00:05:16.326
-[Zooble]: Um, not really.

00:05:16.350 --> 00:05:18.256
-Well, that's not
my problem right now.

00:05:18.280 --> 00:05:19.626
I have an awards show to plan,

00:05:19.650 --> 00:05:22.586
so you guys are gonna have
to handle yourselves for a bit.

00:05:22.610 --> 00:05:24.736
You get five minutes
to figure the teams out.

00:05:24.760 --> 00:05:26.926
Once that's up,
it's a free-for-all.

00:05:30.210 --> 00:05:31.316
-Come on, saddy.

00:05:31.340 --> 00:05:32.916
You're coming with me.
-[gasps]

00:05:32.940 --> 00:05:36.336
I'm... actually gonna be
on a team with Zooble.

00:05:36.360 --> 00:05:37.966
-[Jax]: What?
No, you're not.

00:05:37.990 --> 00:05:41.046
We've been together
for every team adventure in the past.

00:05:41.070 --> 00:05:43.906
-[Zooble]: Guess times
are changing, bunny boy.

00:05:43.930 --> 00:05:45.500
-[grumbles]

00:05:46.540 --> 00:05:49.166
-Hey, you wanna be
on my team?

00:05:49.190 --> 00:05:51.836
-Uh, oh!
I-I'd love to, but --

00:05:51.860 --> 00:05:55.746
Well, uh, I really don't want Kinger
to get stuck with Jax.

00:05:55.770 --> 00:05:57.436
-Oh, yeah.

00:05:57.460 --> 00:06:00.136
Well, I-I could be
on Kinger's team.

00:06:00.160 --> 00:06:01.536
He and I
were together once,

00:06:01.560 --> 00:06:03.156
and it wasn't too bad.

00:06:03.180 --> 00:06:05.520
-U-Uh... Hmm.

00:06:06.310 --> 00:06:09.116
And have... me on...

00:06:09.140 --> 00:06:10.816
-Oh. Um.
Y-yeah.

00:06:10.840 --> 00:06:12.316
Just forget I asked.

00:06:12.340 --> 00:06:13.860
I'll be on Jax's team.

00:06:14.680 --> 00:06:15.856
-W-Wait.

00:06:15.880 --> 00:06:17.400
-Huh?

00:06:17.430 --> 00:06:18.870
-[stammers]

00:06:21.060 --> 00:06:22.906
-Like you said,

00:06:22.930 --> 00:06:25.296
probably good to keep Kinger
and Jax separate.

00:06:25.320 --> 00:06:28.583
I can keep Jax in check,
so don't worry about me.

00:06:30.720 --> 00:06:33.020
-U-Uh, hey, Pomni?

00:06:34.330 --> 00:06:37.886
I-If -- If you ever need
to talk to somebody...

00:06:37.910 --> 00:06:41.500
o-or need help
with anything, I'm here.

00:06:43.070 --> 00:06:44.243
-[laughs weakly]

00:06:45.330 --> 00:06:46.565
[both yelp]

00:06:46.590 --> 00:06:48.936
You have a partner yet?

00:06:48.960 --> 00:06:50.926
-Well, look who it is.

00:06:50.950 --> 00:06:54.496
You sure you can handle me
in all my glory?

00:06:54.520 --> 00:06:56.653
-Eh, I've been through worse.

00:06:57.710 --> 00:06:59.696
-Hey, Zooble?

00:06:59.720 --> 00:07:02.926
Do you wanna hold onto this
during today's game?

00:07:02.950 --> 00:07:03.846
-[Zooble]: Huh?

00:07:03.870 --> 00:07:07.750
-I... don't really trust myself
that much with it.

00:07:08.600 --> 00:07:10.646
And I also just...

00:07:10.670 --> 00:07:13.486
really want to be able
to fire a tommy gun

00:07:13.510 --> 00:07:14.846
while laughing maniacally,

00:07:14.870 --> 00:07:16.986
and I don't --
I don't want to break it

00:07:17.010 --> 00:07:18.790
before I get that chance.

00:07:20.170 --> 00:07:21.930
-[Zooble]: I'll keep it safe for you.

00:07:23.190 --> 00:07:26.716
[dramatic music plays]

00:07:26.741 --> 00:07:29.743
[clock ticking]

00:07:31.660 --> 00:07:33.086
[ding!]

00:07:33.110 --> 00:07:34.356
-Huh?
W-Wait, what?

00:07:34.380 --> 00:07:35.556
That counted?

00:07:35.580 --> 00:07:38.156
-[Zooble]: Uh, Caine?
-What?

00:07:38.180 --> 00:07:40.306
Oh, y-yeah, the guns
have been teleported

00:07:40.330 --> 00:07:42.006
to random spots in the circus.

00:07:42.030 --> 00:07:43.900
Go find 'em, champs.

00:07:45.340 --> 00:07:47.506
-WE NEED TO FIND
THE TOMMY GUN!!!

00:07:47.530 --> 00:07:48.846
-Uh, wait, Caine?

00:07:48.870 --> 00:07:51.056
I-I-I'm missing a life!
-[Kinger]: There's no time!

00:07:51.080 --> 00:07:52.486
-[yelps]

00:07:52.510 --> 00:07:55.226
-It'll be my pleasure
murdering all of you!

00:07:55.250 --> 00:07:57.226
-Uh, have fun, guys!

00:07:57.250 --> 00:07:58.926
-HAH!
You're so lame!

00:07:58.950 --> 00:08:00.950
♪♪

00:08:08.790 --> 00:08:10.340
[dramatic musical sting plays]

00:08:12.770 --> 00:08:14.259
-[Kinger]: Uh-huh.

00:08:14.284 --> 00:08:16.356
Ya little devil.
Alright.

00:08:16.380 --> 00:08:19.946
Now, I would bet our biggest concerns
would be Jax and Zooble.

00:08:19.970 --> 00:08:21.856
They're the youngest,
so they probably still have

00:08:21.880 --> 00:08:23.946
some youthful fighting spirit.

00:08:23.970 --> 00:08:26.096
-[sighs]
Man.

00:08:26.120 --> 00:08:27.946
I'm still missing a heart.

00:08:27.970 --> 00:08:29.906
This isn't fair.
-[Kinger]: Huh?

00:08:29.930 --> 00:08:31.510
Oh, I've got just the thing!

00:08:32.480 --> 00:08:34.396
Here, take this.

00:08:34.421 --> 00:08:35.696
[bing!]
[high tone chimes]

00:08:35.720 --> 00:08:38.686
-W-W-Wait,
what did you just do?

00:08:38.710 --> 00:08:40.036
What was that?

00:08:40.060 --> 00:08:42.996
-[Kinger]: It's a butterfly!
It can restore your health.

00:08:43.020 --> 00:08:45.726
-Did Caine mention that?

00:08:45.750 --> 00:08:47.246
-[Kinger]: Oh, nah.

00:08:47.270 --> 00:08:48.846
I made it up.

00:08:48.870 --> 00:08:49.910
-Uh...

00:08:50.800 --> 00:08:51.890
What?

00:08:54.130 --> 00:08:55.176
[door creaks]

00:08:58.400 --> 00:09:00.686
-So, who you gonna
kill first, Pompom?

00:09:00.710 --> 00:09:05.126
-Uh, I-I don't know if I'll really
be doing much of the killing.

00:09:05.150 --> 00:09:06.856
I-I'll just find guns for you,

00:09:06.880 --> 00:09:09.256
and you can do
all the violent stuff.

00:09:09.280 --> 00:09:10.540
You like that, right?

00:09:11.740 --> 00:09:14.296
-You know none of this
is real, right?

00:09:14.320 --> 00:09:15.756
-[stammers]
What do you mean?

00:09:15.780 --> 00:09:18.506
Like, the circus?

00:09:18.530 --> 00:09:20.956
-The game today
is literally to shoot each other,

00:09:20.980 --> 00:09:24.316
so what's the point
in taking this moral high ground?

00:09:24.340 --> 00:09:26.230
-Well, they're my friends.

00:09:26.260 --> 00:09:28.496
I don't really want to hurt them.

00:09:28.520 --> 00:09:30.120
[bang!]

00:09:30.150 --> 00:09:32.636
-Alright, let me be real here.

00:09:32.660 --> 00:09:34.836
Why do you care about that?

00:09:34.860 --> 00:09:37.846
-Uh, about not hurting my friends?

00:09:37.870 --> 00:09:40.916
-[sighs]
Look, I know what it's like.

00:09:40.940 --> 00:09:43.086
One day, you're somebody
in the real world

00:09:43.110 --> 00:09:44.656
doing important things.

00:09:44.680 --> 00:09:48.686
And then, the next,
you're just a weird little cartoon...

00:09:48.710 --> 00:09:50.056
jester.

00:09:50.080 --> 00:09:51.896
You want to hold onto
that part of you

00:09:51.920 --> 00:09:54.026
that still thinks
it's part of that world,

00:09:54.050 --> 00:09:56.246
but in the end,
what does it get you?

00:09:56.270 --> 00:09:58.656
Ragatha tries to be
all nice and friendly,

00:09:58.680 --> 00:10:01.566
but she gets torn up
every other adventure.

00:10:01.590 --> 00:10:03.126
Whether we like it or not,

00:10:03.150 --> 00:10:06.330
all we are now
is a bunch of cartoon characters.

00:10:07.500 --> 00:10:09.620
So what's the point
of pretending we're not?

00:10:11.070 --> 00:10:14.006
-We're still people though, right?

00:10:14.030 --> 00:10:17.016
-I thought we were at first,
but as time goes on,

00:10:17.040 --> 00:10:19.716
we just end up falling
into our archetypes.

00:10:19.740 --> 00:10:21.596
Become part of the machine.

00:10:21.620 --> 00:10:23.296
-What's your archetype, then?

00:10:23.320 --> 00:10:25.046
The villain?
-[scoffs]

00:10:25.070 --> 00:10:27.366
Listen, I add a key dynamic.

00:10:27.390 --> 00:10:29.266
I see how far
I can push things,

00:10:29.290 --> 00:10:32.516
I screw with people,
and I break the fourth wall.

00:10:32.540 --> 00:10:33.786
You wanna know why?

00:10:33.810 --> 00:10:35.466
It's 'cause it's funny.

00:10:35.490 --> 00:10:37.616
I do everything
'cause it's funny!

00:10:37.640 --> 00:10:39.546
'Cause I'm the funny one.

00:10:39.570 --> 00:10:41.546
-"The funny one"?
-Yeah!

00:10:41.570 --> 00:10:43.126
Ragatha's the cheerful one,

00:10:43.150 --> 00:10:44.636
Gangle's the sad one,

00:10:44.660 --> 00:10:46.176
Kinger's the crazy one,

00:10:46.200 --> 00:10:47.906
Zooble's the grumpy one,

00:10:47.930 --> 00:10:51.626
and you are the one
who hasn't figured that out yet.

00:10:51.650 --> 00:10:54.206
We all just became archetypes.

00:10:54.230 --> 00:10:57.290
I at least have the self-awareness
to choose who I am.

00:10:58.240 --> 00:10:59.956
-The funny one.

00:10:59.980 --> 00:11:01.616
-So, who do you want to be?

00:11:01.640 --> 00:11:04.016
No better chance than now
to try something new.

00:11:04.040 --> 00:11:05.466
You wanna go nuts?

00:11:05.490 --> 00:11:08.776
You wanna finally work off
those weeks of rage and anguish

00:11:08.800 --> 00:11:10.843
that have been
buildin' up inside you?

00:11:11.810 --> 00:11:13.396
I know you hate it here.

00:11:13.420 --> 00:11:14.786
Everyone does.

00:11:14.810 --> 00:11:18.376
But the silver lining is you can
pretty much do whatever you want.

00:11:18.400 --> 00:11:20.316
Like, look at the way
you're aiming that gun.

00:11:20.340 --> 00:11:21.856
Too realistic.

00:11:21.880 --> 00:11:23.280
Just let loose!

00:11:26.520 --> 00:11:28.206
-[inhales deeply]

00:11:28.230 --> 00:11:29.410
[sighs]

00:11:30.430 --> 00:11:31.680
[blam!]

00:11:31.710 --> 00:11:32.730
Huh?

00:11:33.570 --> 00:11:35.406
Oh, what the heck.

00:11:35.430 --> 00:11:38.496
Today, I'm just gonna be evil.

00:11:38.520 --> 00:11:41.176
How's that?
-Heh, go for it!

00:11:41.200 --> 00:11:42.376
-Yeah. Yeah!

00:11:42.400 --> 00:11:45.326
Those other fools
better watch their tails,

00:11:45.350 --> 00:11:48.246
because they're going
to face the wrath

00:11:48.270 --> 00:11:51.196
of Pomni the Evil!

00:11:51.220 --> 00:11:54.630
[laughing malevolently]

00:11:56.000 --> 00:11:58.880
-[scoffs]
It's kinda cringe.

00:12:01.520 --> 00:12:05.126
-Uh, are we really gonna be
shooting each other with these?

00:12:05.150 --> 00:12:06.736
-[Kinger]: It's either shoot or get sh--

00:12:06.760 --> 00:12:08.150
Ah!
-Guh!

00:12:10.050 --> 00:12:11.056
-[Kinger]: Ragatha!

00:12:11.080 --> 00:12:13.336
There's a sniper around this corner.

00:12:13.360 --> 00:12:15.146
-[Zooble]: I think I got Kinger.
[shell clatters]

00:12:15.170 --> 00:12:17.726
-Uh, are you sure we're safe up here?
[gunfire]

00:12:17.750 --> 00:12:19.150
[screams]
-[Zooble]: Whoa!

00:12:20.720 --> 00:12:22.150
-[Kinger]: Tactical roll!

00:12:24.580 --> 00:12:27.656
Come on, Ragatha!
-Mm! [panting]

00:12:27.680 --> 00:12:29.196
[Kinger screaming]
[gunfire]

00:12:29.220 --> 00:12:31.986
-Looks like we've located
the king and the ragdoll.

00:12:32.010 --> 00:12:33.010
-Uh, yeah.

00:12:34.040 --> 00:12:35.516
I mean, yeah!

00:12:35.540 --> 00:12:36.766
Let's get 'em!

00:12:36.790 --> 00:12:37.976
[punchy music plays]

00:12:38.000 --> 00:12:40.896
-Uh, I don't even really know
how to fire a gun.

00:12:40.920 --> 00:12:42.346
I don't know
how much use I'd be in --

00:12:42.370 --> 00:12:43.423
[blam!]

00:12:44.376 --> 00:12:46.106
-Whoops!
Did I do that?

00:12:46.130 --> 00:12:47.796
-You missed a spot!

00:12:47.820 --> 00:12:50.186
-[yelps]
-Hah! You're so cool.

00:12:50.210 --> 00:12:51.790
[gunfire continues]
-[Kinger]: Ragatha, take cover!

00:12:52.750 --> 00:12:54.496
-Huh?
[yelping]

00:12:54.520 --> 00:12:56.106
-I'll take Rags.
You go Kinger.

00:12:56.130 --> 00:12:57.576
-Righty-o, evil bro.

00:12:58.470 --> 00:13:00.586
-I need a gun.
Need a gun, need a gun!

00:13:00.610 --> 00:13:02.120
[exclaims]
[panting]

00:13:02.150 --> 00:13:03.176
-Hah!
-[exclaims]

00:13:03.200 --> 00:13:04.220
[gun clicks]

00:13:05.850 --> 00:13:07.830
Come on, man.
-Hup!

00:13:07.860 --> 00:13:11.026
♪♪

00:13:11.050 --> 00:13:12.976
-[yelping]

00:13:13.000 --> 00:13:14.816
[panting]
Kinger?

00:13:14.840 --> 00:13:17.746
Really use another one
of those butterflies!

00:13:17.770 --> 00:13:19.056
-Howdy, howdy.
-[screams]

00:13:19.080 --> 00:13:22.106
I-I-I know exactly
what you're doing with Pomni,

00:13:22.130 --> 00:13:24.476
and it'll never work!

00:13:24.500 --> 00:13:25.606
-Huh?

00:13:25.630 --> 00:13:29.036
-You know,
getting close with Pomni...

00:13:29.060 --> 00:13:30.740
to corrupt her?

00:13:32.040 --> 00:13:34.126
Wait, no, no, no, no!
Wait, wait, wait!

00:13:34.150 --> 00:13:35.170
[kablam!]

00:13:36.730 --> 00:13:38.106
-[coughs]

00:13:38.130 --> 00:13:41.395
-Oh, wow --
I didn't actually think that'd work.

00:13:41.420 --> 00:13:42.420
[yelps]

00:13:43.780 --> 00:13:45.920
[gun clicking]
-[panting]

00:13:49.020 --> 00:13:50.630
[pop!]
Huh?

00:13:51.913 --> 00:13:52.940
Oh.

00:13:54.300 --> 00:13:57.726
-I lost Kinger,
but I got him down to one life.

00:13:57.750 --> 00:14:00.876
-I lost a life,
but I got us down to one Kinger.

00:14:00.900 --> 00:14:03.566
-How'd you let her
take a life off you?

00:14:03.590 --> 00:14:05.590
-I don't really know.

00:14:11.060 --> 00:14:13.326
-[Zooble]:
Hey, I found this AK... thing.

00:14:13.350 --> 00:14:15.966
If we can't find the tommy gun,
will this work?

00:14:15.990 --> 00:14:17.990
-Uh, yeah.

00:14:19.510 --> 00:14:20.906
Do you...

00:14:20.930 --> 00:14:22.136
think...

00:14:22.160 --> 00:14:23.596
Jax...

00:14:23.620 --> 00:14:26.376
is gonna be mad
that I didn't team up with him?

00:14:26.400 --> 00:14:28.346
-[Zooble]: I wouldn't worry
about him right now.

00:14:28.370 --> 00:14:30.346
It's all just a game,
in the end.

00:14:30.370 --> 00:14:32.706
-It's Jax, though.

00:14:32.730 --> 00:14:34.976
He probably wants revenge.

00:14:35.000 --> 00:14:36.976
And he's gonna
make it painful, and --

00:14:37.000 --> 00:14:39.816
-[Zooble]: Hey, you deserve
better than thinking about him

00:14:39.840 --> 00:14:42.156
when he's not even here.

00:14:42.180 --> 00:14:43.696
You're a human.

00:14:43.720 --> 00:14:45.180
You're not his toy.

00:14:47.990 --> 00:14:51.090
-It sometimes doesn't
feel that way.

00:14:57.230 --> 00:14:59.266
-[Zooble]:
These avatar gimmicks, huh?

00:14:59.290 --> 00:15:01.640
Makes you wonder
why no one else got them.

00:15:02.910 --> 00:15:04.716
-I just wish that...

00:15:05.643 --> 00:15:06.790
[sighs]

00:15:08.050 --> 00:15:12.296
How are you supposed to like
the part of yourself that just...

00:15:12.320 --> 00:15:14.960
makes you worse
than everyone else?

00:15:14.984 --> 00:15:17.715
[melancholy music plays]

00:15:17.740 --> 00:15:20.640
-[Zooble]: 'Cause it exists.

00:15:20.664 --> 00:15:23.285
♪♪

00:15:23.310 --> 00:15:26.226
It's a part of you that's real,

00:15:26.250 --> 00:15:29.406
and the only you
that you should care about

00:15:29.430 --> 00:15:31.210
is the real you.

00:15:31.234 --> 00:15:33.425
♪♪

00:15:33.450 --> 00:15:36.246
You have to choose
to love yourself,

00:15:36.270 --> 00:15:38.636
even if it doesn't make sense.

00:15:38.660 --> 00:15:41.900
It's not natural.
It's intentional.

00:15:43.400 --> 00:15:44.856
-Have...

00:15:44.880 --> 00:15:47.446
you ever had
to make that choice?

00:15:47.470 --> 00:15:49.276
-[Zooble]: Huh?
-S-Sorry.

00:15:49.300 --> 00:15:51.846
I mean... [laughs]
Of course not.

00:15:51.870 --> 00:15:54.470
You're Zooble.
[laughs weakly]

00:15:54.494 --> 00:16:01.494
♪♪

00:16:01.518 --> 00:16:02.726
♪♪

00:16:02.750 --> 00:16:04.036
-[Zooble]: Whatever happens...

00:16:04.060 --> 00:16:06.126
I've got your back
if you've got mine.

00:16:06.150 --> 00:16:07.946
-Yeah.

00:16:07.970 --> 00:16:10.340
Now let's go kill Pomni and Jax.

00:16:11.780 --> 00:16:13.946
-Alright, here's one.

00:16:13.970 --> 00:16:15.596
What's with the corn thing?

00:16:15.620 --> 00:16:17.126
-[scoffs]
What corn thing?

00:16:17.150 --> 00:16:19.126
-Why are you afraid of corn?

00:16:19.150 --> 00:16:20.736
And don't say that you're not.

00:16:20.760 --> 00:16:23.656
You literally jumped out
of your seat twice when you saw some.

00:16:23.680 --> 00:16:26.246
-Heh, not gonna let me
out of this one.

00:16:26.270 --> 00:16:27.670
Well, I dunno.

00:16:27.700 --> 00:16:30.656
It's got a bunch
of little pods on it.

00:16:30.680 --> 00:16:32.356
Looks kind of like an egg sack,
or somethin'.

00:16:32.380 --> 00:16:35.086
It's gross.
Makes my skin crawl.

00:16:35.110 --> 00:16:36.906
-Interesting.

00:16:36.930 --> 00:16:40.136
Do you have, like,
a type of trypophobia?

00:16:40.160 --> 00:16:42.346
-What's that?
-The fear of lots of little holes.

00:16:42.370 --> 00:16:44.546
-Eugh.
-Okay.

00:16:44.570 --> 00:16:47.146
How about... pomegranates?

00:16:47.170 --> 00:16:48.166
-Awful.

00:16:48.190 --> 00:16:50.856
-I'm learning a lot
about you today.

00:16:50.880 --> 00:16:53.656
-Heh, let's not forget
we're here to kill people.

00:16:53.680 --> 00:16:55.606
We still need to find out
where nutso went

00:16:55.630 --> 00:16:57.606
before we can rest easy.

00:16:57.630 --> 00:16:58.650
-[gasps softly]

00:16:59.700 --> 00:17:01.780
-[Kinger]:
I'm right behind you, aren't I?

00:17:02.970 --> 00:17:04.070
[yelps goofily]

00:17:06.130 --> 00:17:07.566
[punchy percussive music plays]

00:17:07.590 --> 00:17:09.656
[gunfire]

00:17:09.680 --> 00:17:16.956
♪♪

00:17:16.980 --> 00:17:19.216
[lighter flicks]
[bullets clinking into cylinder]

00:17:19.240 --> 00:17:20.740
-[Pomni]: There he is!
-[Kinger]: [yelps]

00:17:20.770 --> 00:17:27.040
♪♪

00:17:27.065 --> 00:17:28.535
-[Pomni]: [yelps]
-[Jax]: Whoop, sorry.

00:17:28.560 --> 00:17:32.906
♪♪

00:17:32.930 --> 00:17:36.566
-[Kinger]: I hope you guys are ready
for my ricochet super move!

00:17:36.590 --> 00:17:38.590
[gunfire]
[bullets whizzing]

00:17:42.870 --> 00:17:44.100
-[Jax]: Oh, here's the light.

00:17:45.740 --> 00:17:46.830
-Huh.

00:17:47.790 --> 00:17:49.863
-High-five!
-Yeah!

00:17:49.888 --> 00:17:52.666
[pop!]
-[Kinger]: Ah, what a game.

00:17:52.690 --> 00:17:55.226
Who knew Pomni could be
such a sharpshooter?

00:17:55.250 --> 00:17:57.196
These adventures, huh?

00:17:59.320 --> 00:18:01.446
And look,
even though we lost,

00:18:01.470 --> 00:18:04.280
at least we gave it
our all, right?

00:18:08.520 --> 00:18:11.100
Um... you feeling alright?

00:18:14.450 --> 00:18:16.950
Are you upset that we lost?

00:18:20.180 --> 00:18:23.200
Or are you upset
about something else?

00:18:26.410 --> 00:18:28.160
You wanna talk about it?

00:18:30.970 --> 00:18:32.646
-[sighs]

00:18:32.670 --> 00:18:34.876
[shakily]
I think...

00:18:34.900 --> 00:18:37.470
I might have failed Pomni.

00:18:39.790 --> 00:18:41.870
Just like I failed Jax.

00:18:42.950 --> 00:18:45.146
I try too hard
to get on their good side,

00:18:45.170 --> 00:18:48.766
and then I just end up
pushing them away.

00:18:48.790 --> 00:18:51.046
And then, they end up hating me.

00:18:51.070 --> 00:18:53.166
-[Kinger]: Well, I don't think
anyone in here hates you.

00:18:53.190 --> 00:18:55.336
-[scoffs]
Jax does!

00:18:55.360 --> 00:18:57.185
Gangle and Zooble
don't ever talk to me,

00:18:57.210 --> 00:19:00.696
and Pomni probably won't
after today, either.

00:19:00.720 --> 00:19:01.806
[sighs]

00:19:01.830 --> 00:19:04.666
She came to me
wanting to be on my team.

00:19:04.690 --> 00:19:06.696
I said no.

00:19:06.720 --> 00:19:09.250
[sighs]
Why did I do that?

00:19:10.180 --> 00:19:12.496
-[Kinger]:
Maybe you just needed a break.

00:19:12.520 --> 00:19:15.176
It sounds to me like you put a lot
of pressure on yourself

00:19:15.200 --> 00:19:17.706
to be there for everyone,
and when you're not,

00:19:17.730 --> 00:19:20.196
you beat yourself up for it.

00:19:20.220 --> 00:19:22.826
You said you failed Pomni.

00:19:22.850 --> 00:19:25.280
W-Why do you feel that way?

00:19:26.330 --> 00:19:28.666
-I don't know.

00:19:28.690 --> 00:19:32.176
I feel like every day,
we're drifting further apart.

00:19:32.200 --> 00:19:35.876
Like she's seen through all my tricks
and doesn't trust me anymore.

00:19:35.900 --> 00:19:37.436
Before I know it...

00:19:37.460 --> 00:19:39.316
she'll be a different person.

00:19:39.340 --> 00:19:41.460
One who doesn't even
want me around.

00:19:44.170 --> 00:19:46.066
-[Kinger]: The way I see it,

00:19:46.090 --> 00:19:48.526
relationships are two-sided,

00:19:48.550 --> 00:19:51.246
and sometimes,
it doesn't make sense

00:19:51.270 --> 00:19:52.520
to do all the heavy lifting

00:19:52.550 --> 00:19:54.816
when the other isn't
in the mood.

00:19:54.840 --> 00:19:57.636
We all go through
and deal with things differently,

00:19:57.660 --> 00:19:59.976
and sometimes,
you just need to let people

00:20:00.000 --> 00:20:02.056
do things their own way --

00:20:02.080 --> 00:20:05.466
as long as you're still there
when they need you.

00:20:05.490 --> 00:20:08.616
Giving someone space
should never be the same

00:20:08.640 --> 00:20:10.536
as giving up on them.

00:20:10.560 --> 00:20:13.176
[melancholy music plays]

00:20:13.200 --> 00:20:16.566
-I don't even know
what I want.

00:20:16.590 --> 00:20:19.396
I just want everyone
to be happy.

00:20:19.420 --> 00:20:22.850
And I don't want people
to hate me.

00:20:23.800 --> 00:20:25.636
-[Kinger]: Do you hate yourself?

00:20:25.660 --> 00:20:29.465
♪♪

00:20:29.490 --> 00:20:31.826
I hated myself.

00:20:31.850 --> 00:20:33.506
I couldn't help but hate myself

00:20:33.530 --> 00:20:36.460
for the things I thought
I was responsible for.

00:20:37.420 --> 00:20:39.946
I thought I'd lost everything.

00:20:39.970 --> 00:20:41.256
But then...

00:20:41.280 --> 00:20:43.856
you showed up.

00:20:43.880 --> 00:20:46.776
And my outlook just...

00:20:46.800 --> 00:20:48.100
changed.

00:20:49.150 --> 00:20:51.816
There are always ways
to show you care

00:20:51.840 --> 00:20:54.246
without ruining yourself over it.

00:20:54.270 --> 00:20:58.446
You need to look out for yourself
in all this, too.

00:20:58.470 --> 00:21:00.306
-I don't get it.

00:21:00.330 --> 00:21:02.556
So often, nothing you say
makes any sense.

00:21:02.580 --> 00:21:05.466
But then, you have
these moments where you...

00:21:05.490 --> 00:21:07.556
[laughs]
I don't know.

00:21:07.580 --> 00:21:09.576
How do you do that?

00:21:09.600 --> 00:21:11.536
How've you been around
for so long?

00:21:11.560 --> 00:21:13.166
-[Kinger]: Heh.

00:21:13.190 --> 00:21:15.916
I guess I just have
a resilient mind.

00:21:15.940 --> 00:21:17.556
♪♪

00:21:17.580 --> 00:21:19.310
[music fades out]

00:21:20.790 --> 00:21:22.006
-Breathtaking!

00:21:22.030 --> 00:21:23.890
The committee's gonna love that.

00:21:25.580 --> 00:21:26.880
[punchy, dramatic music plays]

00:21:26.910 --> 00:21:28.976
-[Zooble]:
Are they still following us?

00:21:29.000 --> 00:21:31.276
-Are you still following us?

00:21:31.300 --> 00:21:34.236
-[Jax]: Yeah, we're still following you!
-[Pomni]: Where else would we be?

00:21:34.260 --> 00:21:36.786
-They're still following us.

00:21:36.810 --> 00:21:38.706
-[Zooble]:
Alright, this is a long one.

00:21:38.730 --> 00:21:40.216
We're gonna have to run.

00:21:40.240 --> 00:21:41.280
Let's go!

00:21:42.250 --> 00:21:43.256
-Hah!

00:21:43.280 --> 00:21:50.280
♪♪

00:21:50.304 --> 00:21:51.316
♪♪

00:21:51.340 --> 00:21:54.170
-[Zooble]: Ugh, we got so unlucky
with the drops here.

00:21:55.050 --> 00:21:57.156
-[gasps softly]

00:21:57.180 --> 00:21:58.640
It's time.

00:21:59.690 --> 00:22:00.916
-[Jax]: Why'd you stop shooting?

00:22:00.940 --> 00:22:02.416
You out of ammo?

00:22:02.440 --> 00:22:05.046
-[Zooble]: Why'd you stop?
You out of ammo?

00:22:05.070 --> 00:22:06.436
-Pomni, got any ammo left?

00:22:06.460 --> 00:22:08.666
-Uh, I have one in the cylinder

00:22:08.690 --> 00:22:11.366
and one sniper round,
but no sniper rifle.

00:22:11.390 --> 00:22:12.686
-[scoffs]
Crap.

00:22:12.710 --> 00:22:14.456
-[laughing maniacally]

00:22:14.480 --> 00:22:15.566
-[yelps]

00:22:15.590 --> 00:22:18.236
-[laughing continues]

00:22:18.260 --> 00:22:19.740
Yeah!

00:22:21.440 --> 00:22:23.516
[all hollering]

00:22:23.540 --> 00:22:28.836
♪♪

00:22:28.860 --> 00:22:29.930
-[gasps]

00:22:30.800 --> 00:22:32.000
-[exclaims]
-Ah!

00:22:39.380 --> 00:22:40.440
-[Zooble]: [BLEEP!]

00:22:45.332 --> 00:22:47.246
[lock clicks]
-You're just gonna hide in your room?

00:22:47.270 --> 00:22:48.290
-Coward!

00:22:49.750 --> 00:22:52.530
[parts clicking, snapping]

00:22:54.670 --> 00:22:55.756
-[Zooble]: Huh.

00:22:57.180 --> 00:22:59.616
-[singing]
♪ Daisy ♪

00:22:59.640 --> 00:23:02.006
♪ Daisy ♪

00:23:02.030 --> 00:23:03.846
-[both]: [harmonizing]
♪ Give me your answer, do ♪

00:23:03.870 --> 00:23:05.406
-[Zooble]: Are -- Are you seriously
♪ Give me your answer, do ♪

00:23:05.430 --> 00:23:06.796
gonna start singing that?
♪ Give me your answer, do ♪

00:23:06.820 --> 00:23:11.636
-[both]:
♪ I'm half crazy ♪

00:23:11.660 --> 00:23:15.966
♪ All for the love of you ♪

00:23:15.990 --> 00:23:20.806
♪ It won't be a stylish marriage ♪

00:23:20.830 --> 00:23:25.616
♪ I can't afford a carriage ♪

00:23:25.640 --> 00:23:27.876
♪ But you'll look sweet ♪

00:23:27.900 --> 00:23:30.036
♪ Upon the seat ♪

00:23:30.060 --> 00:23:34.490
♪ Of a bicycle built for two ♪

00:23:35.620 --> 00:23:38.100
-Oh, wait -- I have a key
to Zooble's room.

00:23:40.396 --> 00:23:42.285
[kaboom!]
[grunts] Agh!

00:23:42.310 --> 00:23:44.337
AAAAAAAUGH!!

00:23:44.362 --> 00:23:47.362
[rousing rendition
of "Daisy Bell" plays]

00:23:47.387 --> 00:23:54.387
♪♪

00:23:54.412 --> 00:23:57.670
♪♪

00:23:57.695 --> 00:24:00.346
[groans]
Ugh... ow.

00:24:00.370 --> 00:24:02.156
-I can get 'em.
-W-Wait!

00:24:02.180 --> 00:24:04.440
-Trust me, partner!
I got this!

00:24:06.290 --> 00:24:07.310
-[sighs]

00:24:20.640 --> 00:24:23.616
[dramatic music plays]

00:24:23.640 --> 00:24:30.640
♪♪

00:24:30.664 --> 00:24:33.906
♪♪

00:24:33.931 --> 00:24:35.000
Hah!

00:24:35.030 --> 00:24:40.086
♪♪

00:24:40.110 --> 00:24:42.176
-[Zooble]: That's actual bull-[BOINK!].

00:24:42.200 --> 00:24:43.216
Ow!

00:24:43.240 --> 00:24:47.256
♪♪

00:24:47.280 --> 00:24:48.746
Well, [DOINK!], man.

00:24:48.770 --> 00:24:50.746
Guess that's the end of that.

00:24:50.770 --> 00:24:52.570
See you on the flip side.

00:24:52.595 --> 00:24:55.594
♪♪

00:24:55.619 --> 00:24:57.655
[blam!]
Agh!

00:24:57.680 --> 00:24:58.800
[pop!]

00:25:00.800 --> 00:25:02.336
What?

00:25:02.360 --> 00:25:04.996
-[laughing]

00:25:05.020 --> 00:25:06.236
We did it!

00:25:06.260 --> 00:25:09.106
We made such a good team!
[laughs]

00:25:09.130 --> 00:25:11.146
-Ugh!
-[grunts]

00:25:11.170 --> 00:25:12.276
[stammers]

00:25:13.560 --> 00:25:15.426
-[chuckles]
Well, to be fair,

00:25:15.450 --> 00:25:18.346
our competition
wasn't anything crazy.

00:25:18.370 --> 00:25:20.860
-Eh, yeah, true.

00:25:23.240 --> 00:25:27.646
I suppose this is the part
where one of us betrays the other.

00:25:27.670 --> 00:25:28.680
Hah!

00:25:29.590 --> 00:25:31.176
-Huh?
Oh, yeah.

00:25:31.200 --> 00:25:32.406
You can betray me.

00:25:32.430 --> 00:25:34.526
-Oh.
Uh -- I just --

00:25:34.550 --> 00:25:36.826
I thought this was gonna be
a mutual thing.

00:25:36.850 --> 00:25:38.600
-Nah, nah.
Go on, do it.

00:25:39.560 --> 00:25:42.106
-I-I don't... really want to.

00:25:42.130 --> 00:25:43.676
-La-ame!
Come on!

00:25:43.700 --> 00:25:45.146
I thought you were cool.

00:25:45.170 --> 00:25:48.146
-We could just be winners.

00:25:48.170 --> 00:25:50.366
As a team.
-We're not a team!

00:25:50.390 --> 00:25:51.816
Come on.
-[stammers]

00:25:51.840 --> 00:25:53.116
What do you mean?
Yes, we are.

00:25:53.140 --> 00:25:54.666
-Delusional.

00:25:54.690 --> 00:25:56.976
-W-Weren't we kind of bonding

00:25:57.000 --> 00:25:59.236
over being chaotic-evil together?

00:25:59.260 --> 00:26:01.276
-[scoffs]
I was merely entertaining you

00:26:01.300 --> 00:26:03.336
because I thought it was funny.

00:26:03.360 --> 00:26:05.596
Now, are you gonna
shoot me, or what?

00:26:05.620 --> 00:26:07.506
-Did I... do something wrong?

00:26:07.530 --> 00:26:10.036
-Ugh, you sound like
Ragatha right now.

00:26:10.060 --> 00:26:11.396
No wonder we're not a team.

00:26:11.420 --> 00:26:13.056
-No, I mean --

00:26:13.080 --> 00:26:14.506
We were doing fine.

00:26:14.530 --> 00:26:16.816
Having fun, talking.

00:26:16.840 --> 00:26:18.890
But you suddenly just --
-You're not committing.

00:26:20.090 --> 00:26:21.320
Do it.

00:26:22.580 --> 00:26:23.956
-If I shoot you right now,

00:26:23.980 --> 00:26:25.956
are we still gonna be
friends afterwards?

00:26:25.980 --> 00:26:27.586
-We were never friends.

00:26:27.610 --> 00:26:30.406
-Wh-- What about
all that stuff you told me?

00:26:30.430 --> 00:26:33.186
-Yeah, I did tell you
a lot, didn't I?

00:26:33.210 --> 00:26:35.396
Not looking forward
to thinking about that tomorrow.

00:26:35.420 --> 00:26:36.886
-No. No, no, no.

00:26:36.910 --> 00:26:38.466
We're not doing this.

00:26:38.490 --> 00:26:40.476
You're -- You're not gonna
look me in the eye

00:26:40.500 --> 00:26:42.306
and tell me nothing
we've been doing together

00:26:42.330 --> 00:26:45.460
meant anything to you,
because I know that's not true.

00:26:46.350 --> 00:26:47.806
-Are you coming on to me?

00:26:47.830 --> 00:26:50.830
Yeah, that's what everybody wants --
a straight couple.

00:26:50.860 --> 00:26:53.436
-Oh, my God,
can you take this seriously?

00:26:53.460 --> 00:26:55.666
Can you take anything seriously?

00:26:55.690 --> 00:26:58.376
-Dude, you're a cartoon clown.

00:26:58.400 --> 00:27:00.196
How am I supposed
to take you seriously?

00:27:00.220 --> 00:27:02.196
-Wh-- I --
[exclaims softly]

00:27:02.220 --> 00:27:03.936
You reached out to me,

00:27:03.960 --> 00:27:05.786
not the other way around.

00:27:05.810 --> 00:27:08.306
You're just gonna pretend
that didn't happen?

00:27:08.330 --> 00:27:10.116
-You must be misremembering.

00:27:10.140 --> 00:27:12.356
-Is this why you didn't show up
to Kaufmo's funeral?

00:27:12.380 --> 00:27:14.356
-I don't show up
to ANY funerals.

00:27:14.380 --> 00:27:16.926
-Yeah, I bet you don't --
because you're scared.

00:27:16.950 --> 00:27:20.406
Y-You're scared you'll actually show
a human emotion.

00:27:20.430 --> 00:27:23.046
-I'm scared I'll be
BORED to TEARS.

00:27:23.070 --> 00:27:25.066
-Have you ever thought
that this might be

00:27:25.090 --> 00:27:27.496
what causes people
to abstract in the first place?

00:27:27.520 --> 00:27:29.376
-[laughs bitterly]
Oh, my GOD!

00:27:29.400 --> 00:27:31.226
Are you seriously
gonna blame me for something

00:27:31.250 --> 00:27:33.056
that everybody else did, too?!

00:27:33.080 --> 00:27:34.086
You didn't even know him!

00:27:34.110 --> 00:27:37.356
You don't even know what people are like
before they abstract!

00:27:37.380 --> 00:27:40.516
They are NOT pleasant
to be around --

00:27:40.540 --> 00:27:41.786
like, at all!

00:27:41.810 --> 00:27:43.465
You --

00:27:43.490 --> 00:27:45.176
[scoffs]

00:27:45.200 --> 00:27:47.826
-I-I'm... I'm sorry.

00:27:47.850 --> 00:27:49.850
-[clicks tongue]
I'm sure you are.

00:27:51.150 --> 00:27:53.866
[hisses through teeth]
Hoo, man!

00:27:53.890 --> 00:27:57.070
This is all sorts
of embarrassing, huh?

00:27:57.100 --> 00:27:59.160
So, you gonna
shoot me, or what?

00:28:00.660 --> 00:28:03.480
-What would you do
if I abstracted tomorrow?

00:28:06.890 --> 00:28:08.130
-I'd move on.

00:28:09.670 --> 00:28:11.843
And probably forget about you.

00:28:14.700 --> 00:28:15.800
-Okay.

00:28:18.080 --> 00:28:19.100
Okay.

00:28:21.700 --> 00:28:23.090
I understand.

00:28:27.060 --> 00:28:28.406
-[scoffs]
[chuckles bitterly]

00:28:28.430 --> 00:28:32.040
Geez, you really can't
take a joke, can you?

00:28:34.690 --> 00:28:36.626
-[exclaims]
-[grunts]

00:28:36.650 --> 00:28:38.886
-You're not the funny one!

00:28:38.910 --> 00:28:40.856
-Uh, I don't think that counts.

00:28:40.880 --> 00:28:42.306
-[hollers]
-[grunts]

00:28:42.330 --> 00:28:44.130
-[growling]
-[choking]

00:28:45.950 --> 00:28:47.666
Hey, what are you doing?!

00:28:47.690 --> 00:28:49.126
-[grunting]
-Guh.

00:28:49.150 --> 00:28:50.616
Agh!
-[panting]

00:28:50.640 --> 00:28:51.800
-Guh!
-[chomps]

00:28:53.670 --> 00:28:55.416
-Fight back!
-Are you crazy?!

00:28:55.440 --> 00:28:56.866
-I said, fight back!

00:28:56.890 --> 00:28:58.890
[both grunting, hollering]

00:29:00.940 --> 00:29:01.990
-Stop!

00:29:02.020 --> 00:29:03.930
[both panting]

00:29:06.290 --> 00:29:07.636
What's wrong with you?!

00:29:07.660 --> 00:29:09.946
-Why didn't you fight back?
-Oh, here we go.

00:29:09.970 --> 00:29:11.176
Here we go!

00:29:11.200 --> 00:29:15.026
Because I didn't fight back,
that means I secretly care about you?!

00:29:15.050 --> 00:29:18.056
I'm just a misunderstood
little chicken fetus in an egg

00:29:18.080 --> 00:29:19.466
that needs to be cracked open.

00:29:19.490 --> 00:29:21.916
Well, I am not!

00:29:21.940 --> 00:29:23.376
I do not care about you,

00:29:23.400 --> 00:29:26.406
or anyone else in this circus
in the slightest!

00:29:26.430 --> 00:29:28.776
End of story!

00:29:28.800 --> 00:29:31.336
You are my playthings,

00:29:31.360 --> 00:29:35.806
and I get joy
out of making you suffer.

00:29:35.830 --> 00:29:39.146
I'm the one
who causes pain for fun!

00:29:39.170 --> 00:29:40.886
If I led you on,

00:29:40.910 --> 00:29:44.300
it was just to make this part
hurt you more.

00:29:46.630 --> 00:29:47.630
[BOINK!]

00:29:49.360 --> 00:29:50.360
[DOINK!]

00:29:51.380 --> 00:29:53.196
[panting]

00:29:53.220 --> 00:29:55.220
There's nothing more to me.

00:29:56.430 --> 00:30:00.000
So, please, just stop looking.

00:30:06.740 --> 00:30:09.740
[upbeat fanfare plays]

00:30:09.765 --> 00:30:16.580
♪♪

00:30:16.604 --> 00:30:18.595
♪♪

00:30:18.620 --> 00:30:20.056
[both grunt softly]

00:30:20.080 --> 00:30:22.346
-Hey, I -- I feel like, uh --
-I-I have something I --

00:30:22.370 --> 00:30:24.160
You can speak first.
-No, you go.

00:30:25.510 --> 00:30:27.626
Let's talk after the show.

00:30:27.650 --> 00:30:29.765
-Yeah, sounds good.

00:30:29.790 --> 00:30:35.556
♪♪

00:30:35.580 --> 00:30:37.430
♪♪

00:30:37.455 --> 00:30:40.220
[overlapping chatter]

00:30:45.457 --> 00:30:48.457
[cheers and applause]

00:30:50.140 --> 00:30:52.226
-[Caine]:
Ladies and gentlemen,

00:30:52.250 --> 00:30:56.736
it's time for
the Favorite Character Awards!

00:30:56.760 --> 00:30:59.256
Before anything starts,
I'd like to thank...

00:30:59.280 --> 00:31:00.646
[deep voice]
THE COMMITTEE...

00:31:00.670 --> 00:31:02.016
[normal voice]
for examining our nominees

00:31:02.040 --> 00:31:03.656
and voting on our winners.

00:31:03.680 --> 00:31:05.276
-[Committee Members]:
We love you, Caine!

00:31:05.300 --> 00:31:07.636
-Sh- Shut up.
-[Committee Member]: Okay...

00:31:07.660 --> 00:31:09.216
-[Caine]:
But what's an award show

00:31:09.241 --> 00:31:12.600
without honorable mentions
and subcategories?

00:31:12.625 --> 00:31:14.928
That's right -- it's bad!

00:31:14.953 --> 00:31:17.005
[muffled]
Unlike my show, which is good.

00:31:17.030 --> 00:31:20.030
[muffled music continues]

00:31:20.054 --> 00:31:21.566
♪♪

00:31:21.590 --> 00:31:23.436
-[panting]

00:31:23.460 --> 00:31:25.436
[heartbeat thudding]

00:31:25.460 --> 00:31:27.810
[muffled music fades]
[high-pitched ringing]

00:31:33.560 --> 00:31:34.746
[sighs]

00:31:34.770 --> 00:31:36.766
[muffled music fades in]
[ringing fades out]

00:31:36.790 --> 00:31:39.881
♪♪

00:31:39.906 --> 00:31:42.186
God, you look stupid.

00:31:42.210 --> 00:31:44.206
[toilet flushes]

00:31:44.230 --> 00:31:46.651
♪♪

00:31:46.676 --> 00:31:47.176
-[Disappearing Guy]: So--

00:31:48.970 --> 00:31:53.416
-And the award
for Biggest Sailor Mouth goes to...

00:31:53.440 --> 00:31:54.616
Zooble!

00:31:54.640 --> 00:31:56.616
[cheers and applause]
-[Zooble]: Huh?

00:31:56.640 --> 00:32:03.640
♪♪

00:32:03.664 --> 00:32:05.497
♪♪

00:32:08.700 --> 00:32:13.916
-Alright, folks, it's now the moment
you've all been waiting for...

00:32:13.940 --> 00:32:17.566
the award for Favorite Character!

00:32:17.590 --> 00:32:20.386
Bubble, give me a drum roll.
[drum roll plays]

00:32:20.410 --> 00:32:24.880
-And the award
for Favorite Character goes to...

00:32:25.780 --> 00:32:26.820
Why...

00:32:26.850 --> 00:32:28.990
it's me, everyone!

00:32:33.390 --> 00:32:36.406
Oh, wait, I misread that.

00:32:36.430 --> 00:32:37.716
It's Ming.

00:32:37.740 --> 00:32:42.835
♪♪

00:32:42.860 --> 00:32:45.336
-[Ming]: You shouldn't have
assumed you won the award.

00:32:45.360 --> 00:32:47.360
Now we both look foolish.

00:32:51.683 --> 00:32:54.606
[upbeat jazzy music plays]

00:32:54.630 --> 00:33:01.630
♪♪

00:33:01.654 --> 00:33:08.654
♪♪

00:33:08.678 --> 00:33:16.503
♪♪

00:33:16.528 --> 00:33:18.316
[Captioned by Foulweather Studios]

00:33:18.340 --> 00:33:25.340
♪♪

00:33:25.364 --> 00:33:32.356
♪♪

00:33:40.662 --> 00:33:42.926
-Alrighty.

00:33:42.950 --> 00:33:46.336
Now, let's see how many of them
voted for me.

00:33:49.989 --> 00:33:51.001
Heh.

00:33:51.026 --> 00:33:52.173
[glitched feedback blares]

